    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0663" n="649" xml:id="pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.419/7–1450: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-07-14T12:00:00+01:00">July 14,
                            1950—noon.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>293. Excon. Foreign Office advises that export controls identical those being
                    applied EE countries being placed in effect from today re Communist China for UK
                    exports. Firm position re Hong Kong, Singapore controls promised 5:30 p. m.
                    today. Will cable upon receipt.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d402-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Tomlinson statement reported Embtel 5, July 1, had not been adequately cleared
                    both within Foreign Office and with other government agencies. Fundamental
                    difficulty arose from Foreign Office failure centralize responsibility export
                    control matters which has been source of difficulty throughout discussion re
                    extension controls Far Eastern areas.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 293, repeated info priority Paris 79, priority The Hague 13,
                    priority Brussels 12.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d402-f1" n="1" xml:id="d402-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 319, July 14, 7 p. m., from London (not printed), stated that the
                    British Foreign Office was unable to provide full details ion its decision until
                    Monday (July 17), but the Foreign Office had indicated that there was “no cause
                    for worry” about application of List I controls by Hong Kong and Singapore
                    (493.419/7–1450).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
